    if line == "quit":
        break
```
never breaks even though the file has "quit" on a line

response:
Each line read from a file keeps its trailing newline, so `line` is "quit\n" and never equals "quit". Strip it first:

```python
for line in open("cmds.txt"):
    if line.strip() == "quit":
        break
```

